description:
Company Background

 Our client is a global leader in advanced energy storage solutions, specializing in the design and manufacturing of automotive batteries. Headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, the company serves major automakers and aftermarket retailers, producing over 150 million batteries annually and powering 1 in 3 vehicles worldwide. With operations in more than 50 countries, the company focuses on innovative and sustainable battery technologies for conventional, hybrid, and electric vehicles, supporting the evolving mobility ecosystem.

 Project Description

 The project focuses on an IoT data platform that processes vehicle battery telemetry to detect diagnostic events and support fleet monitoring. We are looking for a Data Platform Engineer to develop and support Python-based streaming services, assist in migrating data processing logic from Snowflake to application code, and contribute to the platform's planned transition to AWS. The specialist will work alongside senior engineers, gaining hands-on experience with event-driven data processing.

 Technologies


 Python

 SQL

 AWS

 Kafka / AWS Kinesis

 Git

 CI/CD


 What You'll Do


 Develop, test, and support production-grade Python streaming services for processing IoT telemetry;

 Assist in migrating Snowflake stored procedures to application code while preserving existing business logic and functionality under the guidance of senior engineers;

 Develop and maintain regression tests, including unit tests;

 Validate migrated business logic by comparing application outputs with data warehouse results;

 Learn and apply event-driven architecture principles, including idempotency, at-least-once delivery, and message ordering;

 Support stateful data processing using Redis or equivalent technologies;

 Develop and deploy small-scale serverless functions and work with AWS object storage services;

 Investigate dropped records and data discrepancies, identify potential root causes, and escalate findings to the team;

 Use Git-based CI/CD pipelines to build, test, and deploy changes;

 Support the planned migration from Azure to AWS and Losant;

 Maintain documentation of findings, system behavior, assumptions, and outstanding questions;


 Job Requirements


 1 - 3 years of professional Python development experience, including writing and testing maintainable code beyond notebooks;

 Strong SQL skills, including joins, aggregations, and window functions, with the ability to understand existing stored procedures;

 Basic understanding of event-driven architecture and messaging concepts (queues, topics, streams), with hands-on experience using Kafka, Event Hubs, Kinesis, or similar technologies through professional work, coursework, or personal projects;

 Working knowledge of Git and willingness to learn CI/CD practices;

 Ability to investigate data discrepancies, compare datasets, and validate results against source data;

 Basic experience with at least one major cloud platform (AWS or Azure);

 Strong written communication and documentation skills;

 English level: B2 or higher;


 Nice To Have


 Experience with Redis or other caching or state management technologies;

 Familiarity with serverless functions (AWS Lambda, Azure Functions) and object storage;

 Understanding of idempotency, at-least-once delivery, and message ordering;

 Experience with Snowflake, including stored procedures and recursive queries;

 Cloud certifications, such as AWS Cloud Practitioner, AWS Solutions Architect Associate, Azure Fundamentals, or Azure Administrator Associate;

 Familiarity with IaC, cloud identity and secrets management, or observability tools;

 Experience with IoT systems or time-series telemetry data;


 What Do We Offer

 The global benefits package includes:


 Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;

 Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;

 Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;

 Health insurance;

 Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;

 Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;

 Referral program for bringing in new talent;

 Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.
